From: Martin Jabůrek <martin.jaburek@suse.com>
Subject: kABI: netfilter: nf_conncount: increase the connection clean up limit to 64
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: CVE-2026-45860 bsc#1266710

Fixing kABI breakage introduced by backporting commit
21d033e472735ecec677f1ae46d6740b5e47a4f3 from upstream.

A new member was added to struct nf_conncount_list as its
last item, in place of previously present padding. The definition
was wrapped in __GENKSYMS__ to denote the kABI change.

Signed-off-by: Martin Jabůrek <martin.jaburek@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Jan Kara <jack@suse.cz>
---
 include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_count.h |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_count.h
+++ b/include/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_count.h
@@ -13,7 +13,9 @@ struct nf_conncount_list {
 	u32 last_gc;		/* jiffies at most recent gc */
 	struct list_head head;	/* connections with the same filtering key */
 	unsigned int count;	/* length of list */
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 	unsigned int last_gc_count; /* length of list at most recent gc */
+#endif
 };
 
 struct nf_conncount_data *nf_conncount_init(struct net *net, unsigned int keylen);
